+A period is given as UTC ISO-8601 strings and is either a whole-day period or an hourly period:
+
+- A whole-day period starts at midnight UTC and ends at midnight UTC on the day after its last day.
+- An hourly period is shorter than a day and starts and ends on the hour. It is priced at the item's
+  hourly price for each hour; `quote` and `book` throw if the item has no hourly price.
+
+`quote` and `book` throw for an unknown item or a period that does not meet either rule; `book` also
+throws if the item is already booked for any part of the period. `availability` throws for a period that
+does not meet either rule or an unknown kind. Cancellation is not implemented yet.
